WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:06.600
Want to play a game? Netflix's smash hit "Squid&nbsp;
Game" is coming back with a vengeance in 2024,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:10.800
and the streaming company's quick teaser&nbsp;
gives us just enough to speculate on.

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:14.920
"Squid Game" took Netflix by storm in&nbsp;
2021, with the South Korean hit becoming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:19.000
the streaming service's most-watched&nbsp;
original series at the time. Since then,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:23.160
fans have been treated to a reality TV spin-off&nbsp;
called "Squid Game: The Challenge" as they wait&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:27.760
for the main show to return. The good news,&nbsp;
however, is that the wait is almost over,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:31.960
as Netflix has released a tantalizing&nbsp;
teaser for "Squid Game" Season 2.

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:36.400
The clip picks up from where the Season 1 finale&nbsp;
left off, as Gi-hun walks through an airport,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:40.440
and he's out for revenge against the Squid&nbsp;
Game's founders. The winner of the titular&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:44.400
deadly competition speaks with one of the&nbsp;
game's mysterious organizers on the phone,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:49.600
who tells Gi-hun that he'll regret the decision to&nbsp;
disobey him. However, Gi-hun isn't intimidated by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:54.160
the threat as he promises to find his enemy&nbsp;
and end the Squid Game once and for all.

00:00:54.160 --> 00:00:58.040
"Squid Game" Season 2 looks set to be&nbsp;
an action-packed and bloody affair that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.040 --> 00:01:01.600
will dig deeper into the lore of&nbsp;
this universe. With that in mind,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:06.280
let's anticipate what we can expect from the&nbsp;
next installment of Netflix's international hit.

00:01:06.280 --> 00:01:11.080
"Squid Game" Season 1 ends with Seong Gi-hun&nbsp;
being financially well-off but feeling more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.080 --> 00:01:16.760
unfulfilled than ever. He learns that his old&nbsp;
friend Contestant 001 is still alive, even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:21.800
though he's terminally ill, and not the humble,&nbsp;
good man he thought he was. It turns out that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:26.720
old man is one of the masterminds behind the Squid&nbsp;
Game, as he and his rich friends created it as a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.720 --> 00:01:32.240
means of entertainment. Naturally, this upsets&nbsp;
Gi-hun, and he isn't willing to stand for it.

00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:37.440
"You put us through all&nbsp;
that… so you could have fun?"

00:01:37.440 --> 00:01:41.560
The Season 2 teaser confirms that Gi-hun will&nbsp;
be out to take down the creators of the deadly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.560 --> 00:01:46.080
game and put a stop to their barbarity.&nbsp;
Sporting a new red hairdo and a desire to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:51.400
end the corruption, Gi-hun has gone from being a&nbsp;
down-on-his-luck everyman to a vengeful warrior,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:56.880
but is he strong enough to stop this entire&nbsp;
operation on his own? Only time will tell.

00:01:56.880 --> 00:02:00.360
While speaking to The Hollywood Reporter,&nbsp;
creator Hwang Dong-hyuk said the next&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:04.280
installment will also explore the backstory&nbsp;
of the man who recruits Gi-hun for the Squid&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.280 --> 00:02:08.800
Game in Season 1. Additionally, he detailed&nbsp;
plans to dig into the story of The Front Man&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:13.480
and Gi-Hun's family history. It remains to be&nbsp;
seen what's in store for viewers, but at least&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.480 --> 00:02:18.145
they won't have long to wait. "Squid Game"&nbsp;
Season 2 will be released sometime this year.

